#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:684
msgid ""
"Both SVE and RVV define sizeless vector types which cannot be used in "
"globals, structs, unions, or arrays. Both provide an attribute "
"(`arm_sve_vector_bits` and `riscv_rvv_vector_bits` respectively) to create "
"fixed-length vector-length-specific (VLS) variants that remove these "
"restrictions. Using these attributes requires the command line option `-msve-"
"vector-bits=<N>` or `-mrvv-vector-bits=<N>` respectively. For SVE, the "
"operators above are supported on both sizeless and VLS types. For RVV, the "
"operators are only supported on VLS types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:693
msgid ""
"See also {ref}`langext-builtin-shufflevector`, {ref}`langext-builtin-"
"convertvector`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:695
msgid ""
"<aside class=\"footnote-list brackets\">\n"
"<aside class=\"footnote brackets\" id=\"id5\" role=\"doc-footnote\">\n"
"<span class=\"label\"><span class=\"fn-bracket\">[</span><a role=\"doc-"
"backlink\" href=\"#id1\">1</a><span class=\"fn-bracket\">]</span></span>\n"
"<p>ternary operator(?:) has different behaviors depending on the condition\n"
"operand's vector type. If the condition is a GNU vector (i.e.,\n"
"<code>__vector_size__</code>), a NEON vector, an SVE vector or an RVV "
"vector,\n"
"it's only available in C++ and uses normal bool conversions (that is, != "
"0).\n"
"If it's an extension (OpenCL) vector, it's only available in C and OpenCL "
"C.\n"
"And it selects based on the signedness of the condition operands (OpenCL "
"v1.1 s6.3.9).</p>\n"
"</aside>\n"
"<aside class=\"footnote brackets\" id=\"vls\" role=\"doc-footnote\">\n"
"<span class=\"label\"><span class=\"fn-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"fn-"
"bracket\">]</span></span>\n"
"<span class=\"backrefs\">(<a role=\"doc-backlink\" href=\"#id2\">1</a>,<a "
"role=\"doc-backlink\" href=\"#id3\">2</a>)</span>\n"
"<p>sizeof can only be used on vector length specific SVE and RVV types.</p>\n"
"</aside>\n"
"<aside class=\"footnote brackets\" id=\"id6\" role=\"doc-footnote\">\n"
"<span class=\"label\"><span class=\"fn-bracket\">[</span><a role=\"doc-"
"backlink\" href=\"#id4\">3</a><span class=\"fn-bracket\">]</span></span>\n"
"<p>Clang does not allow the address of an element to be taken while GCC\n"
"allows this. This is intentional for vectors with a boolean element type "
"and\n"
"not implemented otherwise.</p>\n"
"</aside>\n"
"</aside>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:718
msgid "Vector Builtins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:720
msgid ""
"**Note: The implementation of vector builtins is work-in-progress and "
"incomplete.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:722
msgid ""
"In addition to the operators mentioned above, Clang provides a set of "
"builtins to perform additional operations on certain scalar and vector types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:725
msgid "Let `T` be one of the following types:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:727
msgid ""
"an integer type (as in C23 6.2.5p22), but excluding enumerated types and "
"`bool`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:728
msgid "the standard floating types `float` or `double`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:729
msgid "a half-precision floating point type, if one is supported on the target"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:730
msgid "a vector type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:732
msgid ""
"For scalar types, consider the operation applied to a vector with a single "
"element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:734
msgid ""
"*Vector Size* To determine the number of elements in a vector, use "
"`__builtin_vectorelements()`. For fixed-sized vectors, e.g., defined via "
"`__attribute__((vector_size(N)))` or ARM NEON's vector types (e.g., "
"`uint16x8_t`), this returns the constant number of elements at compile-time. "
"For scalable vectors, e.g., SVE or RISC-V V, the number of elements is not "
"known at compile-time and is determined at runtime. This builtin can be "
"used, e.g., to increment the loop-counter in vector-type agnostic loops."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:742
msgid "*Elementwise Builtins*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:744
msgid ""
"Each builtin returns a vector equivalent to applying the specified operation "
"elementwise to the input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:747
msgid ""
"Unless specified otherwise operation(±0) = ±0 and operation(±infinity) = "
"±infinity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:749
msgid ""
"The elementwise intrinsics `__builtin_elementwise_popcount`, "
"`__builtin_elementwise_bitreverse`, `__builtin_elementwise_add_sat`, "
"`__builtin_elementwise_sub_sat`, `__builtin_elementwise_max`, "
"`__builtin_elementwise_min`, `__builtin_elementwise_abs`, "
"`__builtin_elementwise_clzg`, `__builtin_elementwise_ctzg`, and "
"`__builtin_elementwise_fma` can be called in a `constexpr` context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LanguageExtensions.md:756
msgid ""
"No implicit promotion of integer types takes place. The mixing of integer "
"types of different sizes and signs is forbidden in binary and ternary "
"builtins."
msgstr ""

